1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,800
[SCREAMING]

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
But when a kid walks up…

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:11,500
[GHOST] BOO! Hee hee, gotcha!
…it knows the difference.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
I built a Halloween screen that sees
who's coming up my driveway,

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,500
figures out if they're a kid or an adult,
and picks the right scare.

6
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:22,500
It runs on an old Celeron PC,
it needs no internet,

7
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,000
and you can download it for free.
Link's in the description.

8
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:29,500
Here's what trick-or-treaters see,
from the moment they turn into the driveway.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,500
When nobody's around,
this pumpkin invites people in.

10
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:52,000
[PUMPKIN] Trick or treat! Come on up!

11
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:56,500
The second someone steps into the driveway,
it switches to a welcome.

12
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:00,000
Kids get this cute little ghost.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Adults get glowing eyes in the dark,
and a skull that whispers "come closer."

14
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:09,000
And watch the eyes.
They follow you.

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,500
So how does it know if you're a kid?

16
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:39,500
A small AI model, running right on the PC,
finds people in the camera picture.

17
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:44,000
Then it estimates your real height
from where your feet are.

18
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Under 1.40 metres, you're a kid.

19
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,500
Kids and adults together get the gentle version,
so no little ones get traumatised.

20
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,000
When you get to the candy,
it reminds you: one per person.

21
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,500
[SKULL] One treat per head…
or I take yours.

22
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:21,000
And the moment you reach into the jar…

23
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
[SCREAMING]

24
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:29,000
For kids, it's a big friendly "BOO!"
and a candy explosion.

25
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
For adults…
well, you saw.

26
00:02:40,000 --> 00:03:30,000
[REACTIONS AND LAUGHTER]

27
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Want to build your own?
You need four things,

28
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:38,000
and you probably have them already.

29
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Any Windows PC (mine's a cheap Celeron),
a USB webcam,

30
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:54,000
the biggest screen you've got,
and speakers.

31
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:58,000
No cloud, no subscription,
nothing recorded.

32
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Go to the GitHub page (link in the description)
and click Releases.

33
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Download the Windows zip and unzip it
somewhere permanent, like C:\SpookyTreatStation.

34
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Windows will warn you because it's not
signed by a big company.

35
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Click "More info", then "Run anyway".

36
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:38,000
It's open source,
so anyone can check the code.

37
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Now double-click "Setup Mode"
and pick your camera.

38
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:09,000
Drag the yellow line to where
visitors start counting,

39
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:14,000
the orange line just before your candy,
and the red line right in front of the screen.

40
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Switch on "Watch the candy jar"
and put the blue box over it.

41
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Then have an adult stand far away,
in the middle, and up close,

42
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
and press Capture each time.

43
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:32,000
That teaches it how tall people look
at each distance.

44
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Hit Save, and you're done.

45
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:55,000
You can choose how scary it gets:
mild, medium, or maximum,

46
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:59,000
turn scares off for kids completely,

47
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:04,000
change everything the characters say,
or drop in your own scary videos.

48
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Tip: put the camera at about chest height,
looking down the path.

49
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Turn on a porch light
so it can see at night.

50
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:34,000
And set it to start with Windows,
so it's running when you get home.

51
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:44,000
The link's in the description.

52
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:49,000
If you build one, send me your reactions
and I'll put the best in a follow-up.

53
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:54,000
Happy Halloween…
if you dare.
